For a fixed area, the closer the rectangle is to a **square**, the **smaller** its perimeter.

[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (6,1);
\node[above] at (3,1) {long and thin};
\draw (0,-3.4) rectangle (3,-1.4);
\node[above] at (1.5,-1.4) {closer to a square};
\node[below,font=\small] at (3,-3.7) {The two rectangles have the same area.};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

